      "content": "Attribution to Midnight Typhoon is assessed with HIGH confidence based on: (1) overlap of EclipseRAT C2 infrastructure with previously attributed campaigns NIGHTFALL-23 and DUSK-24, (2) code-level similarities in EclipseRAT with the MoonlightRAT family documented by Mandiant (UNC4491), (3) operational tempo matching Moscow business hours (UTC+3), and (4) target selection consistent with known national intelligence priorities. GAP: No HUMINT corroboration available. SIGINT partially supports via allied partner reporting (TLP:RED, not included in this report).",
      "abstract": "High-confidence attribution to Midnight Typhoon (UNC4491) based on infrastructure, code, and behavioral overlaps.",
      "authors": [
        "Senior Analyst J. Kovalenko",
        "CTI Lead M. Santos"
      ],
      "object_refs": [
        "threat-actor--e5f1b5d0-1a2b-4c3d-8e4f-567890abcdef",
        "intrusion-set--963f1c08-9a8b-45b5-8962-bbbe8e63672f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "opinion",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "opinion--c39efdac-7a22-4cd9-b95d-3fd7ad6f5b4b",
      "created": "2026-02-07T10:00:00.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-02-09T10:00:00.000Z",
      "lang": "en",
      "labels": [
        "peer-review",
        "attribution",
        "allied"
      ],
      "opinion": "agree",
      "explanation": "Our independent analysis of the EclipseRAT samples, C2 infrastructure overlaps, and SIGINT indicators corroborates the HIGH confidence attribution to UNC4491 / Midnight Typhoon. We note additional overlapping indicators from our own case STORM-2491 (TLP:AMBER) that strengthen the assessment.",
      "authors": [
        "Allied CERT — Nordic Cyber Defence Centre"
      ],
      "object_refs": [
        "note--0cb7f6e1-dca6-440e-83a7-b5b694c26b46"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "course-of-action",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "course-of-action--59347ad7-3d1b-4b85-921b-483f4b653747",
      "created": "2026-01-16T10:00:00.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-02-09T10:00:00.000Z",
      "lang": "en",
      "name": "Patch PAN-OS to 10.2.9-h1 or Later",
      "description": "Immediately upgrade all Palo Alto Networks GlobalProtect appliances to PAN-OS version 10.2.9-h1 or later, which contains the fix for CVE-2024-3400. If immediate patching is not possible, apply the vendor-provided mitigation by disabling GlobalProtect device telemetry. Conduct forensic triage of all PAN-OS appliances for signs of exploitation.",
      "labels": [
        "patch",
        "critical",
        "immediate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "course-of-action",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "course-of-action--aed8ae76-b85f-4b53-ba1a-59097adae924",
      "created": "2026-01-20T11:00:00.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-02-09T10:00:00.000Z",
      "lang": "en",
      "name": "Block Eclipse C2 Infrastructure",
      "description": "Add all identified Eclipse C2 domains, IPs, and JA3 fingerprints to network perimeter deny lists. Configure DNS sinkholing for the identified DGA patterns. Enable TLS inspection for DoH traffic to Cloudflare and Google resolvers to detect tunneled C2.",
      "labels": [
        "network",
        "blocking",
        "detection"
      ]
    },
